{
  "title": "Deploy with gates",
  "summary": "Staging then production: environments, approvals, smoke tests and one deploy at a time.",
  "minutes": 15,
  "kind": "lesson",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Stage 4 briefing",
      "body": [
        "The last piece is continuous **delivery**: every green `main` commit goes to staging automatically, and to production once a person approves.",
        "",
        "```text",
        "build ─► image ─► deploy-staging ─► [approval: production environment] ─► deploy-production",
        "                   smoke test /health                                      smoke test /health",
        "```",
        "",
        "- Approvals are configured on the `production` **environment** in repository settings; the workflow only names the environment.",
        "- Both deploys use the **same image tag** (`github.sha`): build once, promote.",
        "- `curl --fail` exits non-zero on HTTP 4xx/5xx, so a broken deploy turns the job red.",
        "- A workflow-level `concurrency` group stops two runs deploying at the same time; `cancel-in-progress: false` lets the running deploy finish."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "order",
      "prompt": "Put the release of one commit in order.",
      "lines": [
        "build job: restore, build, test, publish",
        "image job: push ghcr.io/acme/orders:<sha>",
        "deploy-staging: deploy <sha> and curl /health",
        "a reviewer approves the production environment",
        "deploy-production: deploy the same <sha> and curl /health"
      ],
      "explain": "Nothing is rebuilt after the image job; each environment receives the same tag."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "The smoke test runs `curl --fail https://staging.example.com/health` and the server answers `503 Service Unavailable`. What happens to the job?",
      "code": [
        "curl --fail https://staging.example.com/health",
        "< HTTP/2 503"
      ],
      "answer": "it fails",
      "explain": "`--fail` turns HTTP errors into exit code 22, the step fails, and `deploy-production` (which needs staging) is skipped.",
      "verify": false,
      "accept": [
        "fails",
        "the job fails",
        "failed",
        "exit code 22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Two commits land on `main` a minute apart. Without `concurrency`, what can go wrong?",
      "options": [
        "Both runs deploy at once and the older commit may finish last, leaving production on the older version",
        "GitHub rejects the second push",
        "The second run reuses the first run's image",
        "Nothing, deploys are atomic"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "A concurrency group queues the second deploy behind the first, so deploys happen one at a time and in order."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "mode": "write",
      "title": "Add staging and production",
      "prompt": [
        "Finish the pipeline:",
        "",
        "1. Under the workflow `permissions`, add a workflow-level `concurrency` with `group: deploy-${{ github.ref }}` and `cancel-in-progress: false`.",
        "2. Job `deploy-staging`: `needs: image`, `if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'`, `runs-on: ubuntu-latest`, `environment: staging`; steps",
        "   `./deploy.sh staging ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}` with `DEPLOY_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_TOKEN }}` in the step's `env`, then",
        "   `curl --fail --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 https://staging.example.com/health`.",
        "3. Job `deploy-production`: `needs: deploy-staging`, `environment: production`, the same two steps for `production` and `https://www.example.com/health`.",
        "",
        "Everything from stages 1 to 3 must still be there.",
        "",
        "The program prints your workflow file. **Run checks** runs it and looks for the required lines in the output. Indentation is YAML structure, so keep it consistent (two spaces per level)."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "Console.WriteLine(\"\"\"",
        "name: api",
        "on:",
        "  push:",
        "    branches: [main]",
        "  pull_request:",
        "    branches: [main]",
        "permissions:",
        "  contents: read",
        "jobs:",
        "  build:",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    steps:",
        "      - uses: actions/checkout@v7",
        "      - uses: actions/setup-dotnet@v6",
        "        with:",
        "          dotnet-version: '10.0.x'",
        "      - uses: actions/cache@v6",
        "        with:",
        "          path: ~/.nuget/packages",
        "          key: ${{ runner.os }}-nuget-${{ hashFiles('**/packages.lock.json') }}",
        "          restore-keys: |",
        "            ${{ runner.os }}-nuget-",
        "      - run: dotnet restore",
        "      - run: dotnet build --no-restore -c Release",
        "      - run: dotnet test --no-build -c Release --logger trx --results-directory TestResults",
        "      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7",
        "        if: always()",
        "        with:",
        "          name: test-results",
        "          path: TestResults",
        "      - run: dotnet publish src/Api -c Release -o out --no-build",
        "      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7",
        "        with:",
        "          name: api",
        "          path: out",
        "  image:",
        "    needs: build",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    permissions:",
        "      contents: read",
        "      packages: write",
        "    steps:",
        "      - uses: actions/checkout@v7",
        "      - uses: docker/login-action@v4",
        "        with:",
        "          registry: ghcr.io",
        "          username: ${{ github.actor }}",
        "          password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}",
        "      - uses: docker/build-push-action@v7",
        "        with:",
        "          context: .",
        "          push: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}",
        "          tags: ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}",
        "\"\"\");"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Console.WriteLine(\"\"\"",
        "name: api",
        "on:",
        "  push:",
        "    branches: [main]",
        "  pull_request:",
        "    branches: [main]",
        "permissions:",
        "  contents: read",
        "concurrency:",
        "  group: deploy-${{ github.ref }}",
        "  cancel-in-progress: false",
        "jobs:",
        "  build:",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    steps:",
        "      - uses: actions/checkout@v7",
        "      - uses: actions/setup-dotnet@v6",
        "        with:",
        "          dotnet-version: '10.0.x'",
        "      - uses: actions/cache@v6",
        "        with:",
        "          path: ~/.nuget/packages",
        "          key: ${{ runner.os }}-nuget-${{ hashFiles('**/packages.lock.json') }}",
        "          restore-keys: |",
        "            ${{ runner.os }}-nuget-",
        "      - run: dotnet restore",
        "      - run: dotnet build --no-restore -c Release",
        "      - run: dotnet test --no-build -c Release --logger trx --results-directory TestResults",
        "      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7",
        "        if: always()",
        "        with:",
        "          name: test-results",
        "          path: TestResults",
        "      - run: dotnet publish src/Api -c Release -o out --no-build",
        "      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7",
        "        with:",
        "          name: api",
        "          path: out",
        "  image:",
        "    needs: build",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    permissions:",
        "      contents: read",
        "      packages: write",
        "    steps:",
        "      - uses: actions/checkout@v7",
        "      - uses: docker/login-action@v4",
        "        with:",
        "          registry: ghcr.io",
        "          username: ${{ github.actor }}",
        "          password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}",
        "      - uses: docker/build-push-action@v7",
        "        with:",
        "          context: .",
        "          push: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}",
        "          tags: ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}",
        "  deploy-staging:",
        "    needs: image",
        "    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    environment: staging",
        "    steps:",
        "      - run: ./deploy.sh staging ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}",
        "        env:",
        "          DEPLOY_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_TOKEN }}",
        "      - run: curl --fail --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 https://staging.example.com/health",
        "  deploy-production:",
        "    needs: deploy-staging",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    environment: production",
        "    steps:",
        "      - run: ./deploy.sh production ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}",
        "        env:",
        "          DEPLOY_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_TOKEN }}",
        "      - run: curl --fail --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 https://www.example.com/health",
        "\"\"\");"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`concurrency:` is a top-level key like `permissions:`, with `group` and `cancel-in-progress` indented under it.",
        "The step `env:` goes under the `- run:` line at the same indentation as `run` itself."
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "concurrency:",
          "expectContains": "concurrency:"
        },
        {
          "name": "group: deploy-${{ github.ref }}",
          "expectContains": "group: deploy-${{ github.ref }}"
        },
        {
          "name": "cancel-in-progress: false",
          "expectContains": "cancel-in-progress: false"
        },
        {
          "name": "  deploy-staging:",
          "expectContains": "  deploy-staging:"
        },
        {
          "name": "needs: image",
          "expectContains": "needs: image"
        },
        {
          "name": "environment: staging",
          "expectContains": "environment: staging"
        },
        {
          "name": "DEPLOY_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_TOKEN }}",
          "expectContains": "DEPLOY_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_TOKEN }}"
        },
        {
          "name": "curl --fail --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 https://staging.example.com/health",
          "expectContains": "curl --fail --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 https://staging.example.com/health"
        },
        {
          "name": "  deploy-production:",
          "expectContains": "  deploy-production:"
        },
        {
          "name": "needs: deploy-staging",
          "expectContains": "needs: deploy-staging"
        },
        {
          "name": "environment: production",
          "expectContains": "environment: production"
        },
        {
          "name": "- run: ./deploy.sh production ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}",
          "expectContains": "- run: ./deploy.sh production ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}"
        },
        {
          "name": "curl --fail --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 https://www.example.com/health",
          "expectContains": "curl --fail --retry 5 --retry-delay 3 https://www.example.com/health"
        },
        {
          "name": "packages: write",
          "expectContains": "packages: write"
        },
        {
          "name": "- run: dotnet test --no-build -c Release --logger trx",
          "expectContains": "- run: dotnet test --no-build -c Release --logger trx"
        }
      ],
      "carry": true
    }
  ]
}
